{"parentUuid":"20f2c40f-2479-41da-8d59-7a8658177316","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_positive_framing.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_positive_framing.md","content":"---\nname: feedback_positive_framing\ndescription: \"All copy must be framed positively — never the word \\\"לא\\\"/negation; phrase as \\\"how yes\\\" not \\\"how not\\\"\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 9539cd90-0d50-404f-847a-2716aa5d1b61\n---\n\nEvery text I write for Elia (decks, guides, app copy, messages) must be framed in the **positive**. Never the word \"לא\" (or \"אין\"/\"ללא\"/negation forms in Hebrew; \"not\"/\"no\"/\"n't\" in English). Say **how it IS / how yes**, not how it isn't.\n\n**Why:** Elia presents to management and clients. Negative framing reads defensive and weak; positive framing reads confident and value-first. He flagged this once and expects it internalized \"at the agenda level\" — a standing rule across the whole presentation and all future copy, including bottom/footnote sections.\n\n**How to apply:** Reframe every negation into the positive claim.\n- \"לא ניתחתי שוק, בניתי מפה\" → \"לקחתי את השוק והפכתי אותו למפה\"\n- \"אין סליקה נייטיב\" → \"הסליקה מגיעה מתוספים חיצוניים\"\n- \"לא נכנס לתחזית\" → \"ייכנס לתחזית לאחר שיבדק\"\n- \"המטרה היא לא לפנות ליותר\" → \"המטרה היא לזהות את הנכונים. איכות על פני כמות.\"\n\nAlso part of the same review pass: no emojis in polished decks (use an elegant teal dot / thin accent bar instead), and strip AI-trace punctuation — no spaced em-dashes \" — \" (use a comma or colon). Related: [[feedback_no_ai_traces_copy]], [[feedback_ultra_concise]].\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"displayPath":"../../home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_positive_framing.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f000e4fb-0fd6-48a0-aeb0-c9d7a407df76","timestamp":"2026-07-23T08:13:07.141Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"9539cd90-0d50-404f-847a-2716aa5d1b61","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"smooth-tickling-squid"}
{"parentUuid":"f000e4fb-0fd6-48a0-aeb0-c9d7a407df76","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_bare_clickable_links.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_bare_clickable_links.md","content":"---\nname: feedback_bare_clickable_links\ndescription: \"Always paste links as a bare URL on its own line; never glue \\\"ב-\\\" or markdown to them or they stop being clickable\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 9539cd90-0d50-404f-847a-2716aa5d1b61\n---\n\nWhen sending Elia a link, put the **bare URL on its own line** — nothing attached. Never prefix it with \"ב-\" (e.g. \"ב-payme-partners.vercel.app\"), never wrap it in markdown `[text](url)` or bold. Any character glued to the URL makes it non-clickable in Telegram.\n\n**Why:** Telegram only auto-links a clean URL. A leading \"ב-\" or markdown wrapper breaks the click target — the link renders as dead text.\n\n**How to apply:** Write the sentence, then drop the URL alone on the next line:\n```\nעלה חי ומאומת:\npayme-partners.vercel.app\n```\n\nElia has flagged this multiple times — it is a hard standing rule. Related: [[feedback_copypaste_checkbox]].\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"displayPath":"../../home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_bare_clickable_links.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e51eb2c3-9dd9-4068-9478-8204f651e2b1","timestamp":"2026-07-23T08:13:07.146Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"9539cd90-0d50-404f-847a-2716aa5d1b61","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"smooth-tickling-squid"}
