pp end to end, using the standard channel registration — no manual glue per message.</p>\n\n<h3>Phase 5 — Harden for a short pilot</h3>\n<p>Handle: reconnect after network drop; media / voice inbound at least gracefully (transcribe or acknowledge); long-message and formatting correctness; and ban-risk hygiene — warm the number slowly, message only opted-in testers, never bulk-blast, since unofficial numbers get permanently banned on spam patterns. Back up the session / auth state.</p>\n<p><b>DONE-TEST (V6):</b> run a 10-message mixed conversation (text plus one media) across a reconnect; all handled without crash or lost context; auth state backed up and documented.</p>\n\n<h2>&lt;definition_of_done&gt;</h2>\n<p>All of V1–V6 green, and a real person on a normal phone holds a genuine back-and-forth with a NanoClaw agent over WhatsApp on a dedicated number, with zero visibility of those chats in Elia's personal WhatsApp.</p>\n\n<h2>&lt;final_report&gt;</h2>\n<p>When done, write back in this exact structure:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>What existed vs. what you built (the Phase 0 finding first).</li>\n<li>Exact files added or changed.</li>\n<li>The dedicated-number setup: number type, how paired, where session state lives, how to swap the number.</li>\n<li>How to start / stop it safely (the single-instance rule).</li>\n<li>The privacy proof statement (V4).</li>\n<li>Known limits plus the honest ban-risk note, and the concrete next step to production (Cloud API via 360dialog: dedicated API-only number, webhook on the existing provision tunnel, pre-approved templates, per-message pricing).</li>\n<li>Anything you were blocked on and exactly what you need from Elia (most likely: the dedicated SIM / eSIM number to pair).</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>&lt;key_facts&gt;</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Personal-number link = owner sees all chats → FORBIDDEN. Dedicated number only.</li>\n<li>VoIP numbers (Google Voice, TextNow) are rejected by WhatsApp verification; data-only travel eSIMs (Airalo) cannot receive the 