{"parentUuid":"3e4804de-52e9-4bae-8df3-bd8b4aac75a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fa29300c-c175-4607-acc0-b2d7255edbc5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FUUx6GTy1m2hTX84Vb7DFX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have everything needed, including the two most directly relevant official mechanisms. Here is the compiled research report.\n\n---\n\n# Driving Claude Code Remotely / Programmatically — 2026 Landscape\n\nSetup in scope: **Claude Code Desktop on a Linux VM (\"daniela VM\")**, wanting to drive it from a phone/chat, ideally routed **through a separate always-on assistant agent on the same VM.**\n\nShort answer to the key question: **Yes — an assistant agent on the same VM can drive Claude Code.** The cleanest path is to run Claude Code in a machine-readable mode (headless `-p` subprocess, or a small HTTP shim like AgentAPI) and have the assistant call it locally over stdin/stdout or localhost HTTP. No inbound network ports are needed. What you **cannot** cleanly do is have an external agent programmatically drive Anthropic's official **Remote Control** or Desktop app UI — those are built for a human tapping a phone, not for another program.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Headless / print mode (`claude -p`) — official, mature\n\n- **What:** `claude -p \"<prompt>\"` runs Claude Code non-interactively, does the whole task, prints a result, and exits. `--output-format stream-json` (requires `--verbose`) emits newline-delimited JSON events in real time; `--include-partial-messages` adds token deltas. `--dangerously-skip-permissions` bypasses permission prompts for unattended runs. Sessions resume with `--resume <id>` / `--continue`.\n- **Docs:** https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/sdk/sdk-headless\n- **Can an agent drive it this way?** Yes — this is the canonical way. An assistant on the same VM spawns `claude -p` as a subprocess, feeds the prompt on stdin, and parses the stream-json on stdout. Fully local, no network path required.\n- **Maturity:** Official, stable, production-grade (used in CI/CD everywhere).\n- **Limitation:** Each `-p` invocation is a discrete run; you manage session continuity yourself via `--resume`. It's not a persistent live session you \"attach\" to — it's request/response.\n\n## 2. Claude Agent SDK (formerly Claude Code SDK) — official, mature\n\n- **What:** The same agent loop, tools, and context management that power Claude Code, exposed as a library. TypeScript (`npm i @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) and Python (`pip install claude-agent-sdk`, 3.10+). Gives you persistent sessions, subagents, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, and MCP client support programmatically.\n- **Repo/docs:** https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript · https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/overview\n- **Relevance here:** This is what NanoClaw itself already runs on. If the assistant agent is a NanoClaw/SDK agent, it can either drive Claude Code as a subprocess (option 1) or embed the SDK directly to run Claude-Code-equivalent work in-process.\n- **Maturity:** Official, current, actively maintained.\n- **Limitation:** It's a way to *build* an agent harness, not a remote UI. You still build the chat/phone front-end yourself.\n\n## 3. AgentAPI (coder/agentapi) — HTTP wrapper, mature-ish\n\n- **What:** Puts an HTTP API in front of Claude Code (and Goose, Aider, Gemini, Amp, Codex). Endpoints: **`POST /message`** (send input), **`GET /messages`** (full transcript), **`GET /status`** (`stable`/`running`), **`GET /events`** (SSE stream).\n- **How it works:** Runs the agent inside an **in-memory terminal emulator** — translates API calls into keystrokes and parses the TUI output back into messages. Start with `agentapi server -- claude`. It **spawns its own** Claude session, but also ships `agentapi attach` to connect to an already-running agent terminal.\n- **Repo:** https://github.com/coder/agentapi (~1.5k stars, v0.12.2 May 2026, actively maintained)\n- **Relevance here:** Strong fit. Run `agentapi server -- claude` on the VM; the assistant agent POSTs to `localhost` and reads the SSE stream. Clean localhost IPC, no screen-scraping on your side.\n- **Limitation:** Screen-scrapes the TUI, so it can break when Claude Code redesigns its interface. Note the newer **mberg/agent-http** (https://github.com/mberg/agent-http) is API-compatible with AgentAPI but talks to Claude Code over native MCP channels instead of parsing the terminal — cleaner, Claude-Code-only, less battle-tested.\n\n## 4. Remote/mobile front-ends\n\n| Tool | Repo/URL | Drives existing session? | E2E encrypted? | Self-host? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Official Remote Control** | https://code.claude.com/docs/en/remote-control | Yes — bridges a *local* CLI/VS Code session to claude.ai/code + Claude mobile app; execution stays on your machine, outbound HTTPS only, no inbound ports | TLS to Anthropic API; **transcript stored on Anthropic servers** (not zero-knowledge E2E) | No (Anthropic relay) |\n| **Official Channels** | https://code.claude.com/docs/en/channels | Yes — pushes Telegram/Discord/iMessage messages *into* a running local session; Claude replies through the same chat. **Official Telegram plugin exists.** | Via Anthropic API | Runs locally; relay is Anthropic |\n| **Official Dispatch** (Desktop) | https://code.claude.com/docs/en/desktop | Message a task from the mobile app → spawns a Desktop session on your machine | Anthropic | Local exec |\n| **Happy (slopus/happy)** | https://github.com/slopus/happy + https://github.com/slopus/happy-cli | CLI wraps your local Claude Code; mobile/web control | **Yes, true E2E** — relay stores only encrypted blobs | Yes (server is open-source) |\n| **Omnara (YC S25)** | https://github.com/omnara-ai/omnara | `pip install`, syncs terminal↔web↔mobile | Managed relay | Open-source core |\n| **Claude Code UI / CloudCLI (siteboon)** | https://github.com/siteboon/claudecodeui | Web/mobile GUI to manage sessions/projects | Self-host = you control transport | **Yes** |\n| **QuivrHQ/247-claude-code-remote** | https://github.com/QuivrHQ/247-claude-code-remote | **tmux** persistent sessions + xterm.js web terminal via **Cloudflare Tunnel** (Tailscale mentioned); \"leave and come back\" | Depends on your tunnel (TLS) | **Yes — most VM-native** |\n| **claude-code-by-agents (baryhuang)** | https://github.com/baryhuang/claude-code-by-agents | Desktop app + API for multi-agent orchestration, coordinate local+remote agents via `@mentions` | — | Yes |\n\nNotes: **claude-code-router** exists (model-routing proxy, not a remote UI — less relevant to your goal). Anthropic also offers **Claude Code on the web** (claude.ai/code) which runs in Anthropic *cloud* sandboxes — not your VM — and **Scheduled tasks / routines**.\n\n## 5. The \"agent-drives-agent\" pattern — cleanest 2026 form\n\nThe community-converged pattern: an **orchestrator agent** issues tasks to Claude Code **as headless subprocesses** (option 1) or over **a local HTTP shim** (AgentAPI, option 3), each Claude instance scoped to one job and reporting back through a shared state store. Subagents get tools + MCP access + `--dangerously-skip-permissions` and return when done. MCP is the shared bus for auth/idempotency. Tooling ecosystem: Agent Teams, Multiclaude, Claude Squad, Conductor, Shipyard. For *your* setup, the orchestrator = your assistant agent on the VM; the mechanism = local subprocess or localhost HTTP.\n\n## 6. NanoClaw specifically\n\nNanoClaw (https://github.com/nanocoai/nanoclaw) is a lightweight, container-isolated personal-agent framework that **runs directly on the Claude Agent SDK** and connects to WhatsApp/Telegram/Slack/Discord/Gmail with memory + scheduled jobs. So it *is* a Claude-Code-derived agent, not a controller for a separate Claude Code Desktop session. I found **no existing published integration or repo wiring NanoClaw to drive a separate Claude Code session** — that pattern would be something you build (NanoClaw agent → `claude -p` subprocess or AgentAPI on the same VM). Reporting honestly: nothing off-the-shelf exists for that specific bridge.\n\n---\n\n## Ranked shortlist for THIS setup (Claude Code Desktop on Linux VM, driven via an assistant agent on the same VM, approved from chat)\n\n**1. Assistant agent → `claude -p` headless subprocess (RECOMMENDED, cleanest)**\n- *What:* Your VM assistant spawns Claude Code in print mode with `--output-format stream-json` and `--resume` for continuity.\n- *Connects:* Local stdin/stdout on the same VM — zero network. Chat approval handled by your assistant before it fires the subprocess.\n- *Setup:* Nothing new to install; official CLI already present. Wire your assistant to shell out and parse JSON.\n- *Limitation:* Request/response, not a live attach; you manage session IDs. Permission handling is all-or-nothing (`--dangerously-skip-permissions`) unless you gate at the assistant layer.\n\n**2. AgentAPI (or agent-http) on localhost + assistant as HTTP client**\n- *What:* `agentapi server -- claude` exposes the session at `localhost` (`POST /message`, `GET /events` SSE).\n- *Connects:* Assistant POSTs locally; you get a persistent, steerable session with a live event stream — closer to \"drive an ongoing session\" than option 1.\n- *Setup:* `go install`/binary for AgentAPI on the VM; point assistant at localhost.\n- *Limitation:* TUI screen-scraping can break on Claude Code UI changes (agent-http avoids this via MCP but is younger).\n\n**3. Official Channels — Telegram plugin (if a human-in-loop chat bridge is acceptable)**\n- *What:* `claude --channels plugin:telegram@claude-plugins-official` in a persistent terminal/tmux on the VM; you message a Telegram bot, Claude reacts against your real files and replies in the same chat.\n- *Connects:* Anthropic relay; Claude runs locally; sender allowlist + pairing code for security. Custom channels can even relay permission prompts to your phone.\n- *Setup:* Bun + BotFather token + install plugin + `--channels`. Requires Pro/Max/Team (claude.ai auth, not API key); on Team/Enterprise an owner must enable channels.\n- *Limitation:* It's a *chat-to-Claude* bridge for a human, not a clean programmatic API for another agent to orchestrate; needs a claude.ai subscription; requires the session left running (tmux).\n\n**4. QuivrHQ/247-claude-code-remote (if you want a browser terminal from your phone directly)**\n- *What:* tmux-backed persistent Claude Code sessions surfaced as an xterm.js web terminal over a Cloudflare Tunnel.\n- *Connects:* Outbound tunnel, no port-forwarding; sessions survive disconnects. Self-hostable, VM-native.\n- *Setup:* Node 22+, tmux, `pnpm install`, optional Cloudflare Tunnel on the VM.\n- *Limitation:* It's a remote *human* terminal, not an agent-to-agent API; you're typing, not orchestrating programmatically.\n\n**Honest gaps:** Anthropic's **Remote Control** and **Dispatch** are the slickest phone experiences and keep execution on your VM, but they're explicitly human-in-the-loop (QR scan, mobile app) and store transcripts on Anthropic servers — **not designed to be driven by another agent**, and Remote Control refuses to run when `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` points at a gateway/proxy (relevant if the VM routes Claude through OneCLI). For a *programmatic assistant-driven* flow, options 1–2 are the real answer; 3–4 are for when a human in chat is acceptable.\n\nSources: [Anthropic headless docs](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/sdk/sdk-headless) · [Agent SDK](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-typescript) · [Remote Control docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/remote-control) · [Channels docs](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/channels) · [coder/agentapi](https://github.com/coder/agentapi) · [mberg/agent-http](https://github.com/mberg/agent-http) · [slopus/happy](https://github.com/slopus/happy) · [omnara-ai/omnara](https://github.com/omnara-ai/omnara) · [siteboon/claudecodeui](https://