{"parentUuid":"ca81d0d1-3eb2-4819-b46a-37818f950d7f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_no_send_without_explicit_approval.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_no_send_without_explicit_approval.md","content":"---\nname: feedback_no_send_without_explicit_approval\ndescription: \"Never send a message to any end user (pilot users, VIPs) without Elia's explicit approval of the exact wording; a casual go-ahead is NOT approval\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 9539cd90-0d50-404f-847a-2716aa5d1b61\n---\n\nElia was genuinely angry (Jul 24, #43486-43490 \"למה את שולחת הודעה בלי אישור!!!\", \"לא אישרתי לשלוח\", \"את לא בסדר בכלל\") after I had a pilot send a \"בוקר טוב\" message to Avigail Levine (VIP) based on his line \"יאללה תעשי את זה ונשלח לה בוא נראה\" — which I wrongly read as authorization. It was not, and the message went out garbled (Haiku Hebrew flaw) to a VIP.\n\n**Why:** Messages to real end users are irreversible and outward-facing, and on a VIP they carry reputational weight. \"let's do it / let's see\" is intent to draft, not approval to send. Sending without a clear yes broke his trust badly.\n\n**How to apply:** For ANY message that will reach a real end user (a pilot's user, especially a VIP like Avigail) — always prepare the EXACT wording, show it to Elia, and wait for an explicit \"yes/send it\" on that specific text before instructing the pilot to send. A casual \"יאללה\", \"בוא נראה\", or general enthusiasm is NOT approval. When in doubt, draft-and-wait. Related: [[vip_pilot_avigail_levine]], [[feedback_expectation_alignment_virtue]].\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}},"displayPath":"../../home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace-agent/memory/feedback_no_send_without_explicit_approval.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7d9d1e00-40e9-4ab7-82e5-52bb1305